## Why This Is Asked
Tests solving interdependent CV tasks under tight latency with on-device adaptation for unseen objects, in realistic cluttered scenes.

## Key Concepts
- Shared backbone with multi-head decoders
- Joint losses: depth, normals, affordance, temporal consistency
- 5-shot on-device adaptation for novel objects
- Edge-GPU constraints (<25 ms) and robustness to occlusion/dynamic lighting

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-architecture wiring
function forward(x) {
  const z = encoder(x);
  const d = depthHead(z);
  const n = normalsHead(z);
  const a = affordanceHead(z);
  return { depth: d, normals: n, affordances: a };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you diagnose a failing grasp affordance map with occlusion?
- What ablations would you run to validate the importance of temporal consistency?

## Why This Is Asked
Introduces a new angle: multi-sensor fusion with event cameras for high-dynamic scenes. Assesses architectural discipline and concrete trade-offs for low latency and on-device adaptation.

## Key Concepts
- Event cameras and RGB fusion
- 3D voxel grids and lightweight transformers
- On-device 5-shot adaptation and object priors
- Temporal consistency and occlusion handling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo code: fuse RGB features with events, then predict pose and mask
function forward(rgbFrame, events, priors){
  const rgbFeat = rgbBackbone(rgbFrame);
  const evtFeat = eventBackbone(events);
  const fused = fuse3D(rgbFeat, evtFeat);
  const pose = poseHead(fused, priors);
  const mask = segHead(fused);
  return {pose, mask};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you design synthetic data generation to cover unseen shapes with realistic event streams?
- What debugging metrics would help you diagnose latency vs. accuracy bottlenecks on edge hardware?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a complete edge-CV pipeline: real-time monocular 3D pose with per-object velocity, occlusion robustness, and rapid on-device adaptation to unseen parts. Emphasizes practical data strategies and evaluation in an industrial setting.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time monocular 3D pose estimation
- Per-instance velocity prediction for planning
- On-device few-shot adaptation (5-shot)
- Occlusion handling and data fusion strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: forward pass with adaptation trigger
function forward(frame, exemplars){
  let features = backbone(frame);
  let detections = detector(features);
  let poses = poseHead(features, detections);
  let vel = velocityHead(features, detections, previous);
  if (exemplars) adapt(poses, exemplars);
  return {detections, poses, vel};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify robustness to occlusion in your evaluation?
- What ablation would you run to isolate the velocity head contribution?
